      "writtenOn": "2023-10-27T09:21:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While I think this is correct, I don\u0027t think this is the most readable form for computing this. In particular, `maskShouldDrop` will have 1s for all bits that are not part of any chain, which is pretty confusing (it\u0027s removed by the \u0026 with maskEnabledChain below, so it\u0027s still correct).\n\nI think the following would be easier to follow.\n\n    final boolean denied \u003d 0 !\u003d uidRuleConfig \u0026 ~uidMatch \u0026 sMaskDropIfUnset;\n    final boolean allowed \u003d 0 !\u003d uidRuleConfig \u0026 uidMatch \u0026 sMaskDropIfSet;\n    return allowed \u0026\u0026 !denied;\n\nThis is like 1 more binary operation, which is completely negligible compared to the allocation in l.229.",
      "range": {
